## 2. Algorithm (do not invent)

Match existing `aether_uf_peel` / `peeling.rs` semantics:

1. Build solid adjacency (Gr-Gen edge list → undirected adj).
2. BFS spanning forest on solid edges (discard back-edges).
3. Per component: order nodes; **M10** root = boundary in component if any, else a degree-1 node.
4. Peel leaves toward root; `corr` from frozen syndrome bits.

**Change:** stages that previously ran a full BFS/stack in **one** clock now take **one queue/stack pop per clock** (Das Corr is multi-cycle by nature).

---

## 3. FSM sketch

| State | Work / cycle |
| --- | --- |
| IDLE→capture | Load packed buses |
| BUILD_CLR | Clear tables (node/edge index) |
| BUILD_E | One solid edge → dual adj push |
| F_SEEK / F_BFS | Seek unvisited start; one BFS pop + neighbor expand |
| R_CLR / R_SEEK / R_WALK / R_PICK | Clear visited; stack walk one pop; assign peel_root |
| SEED | Enqueue degree-1 non-roots |
| PEEL | One peel op (unchanged) |
| DONE | `done` |

Packed ports unchanged (M59).

